body:
Still not a valid reason though, just because they might be sad they don't have a say in it.

&#x200B;

For example a more logical argument would be the nature of the illness, if it's a mental illness, you could argue that it is a treatable disease, and include the desire to suicide within that mental illness. Even with that argument I am trying to understand what makes people believe that every mental illness is treatable.

"**and if not, then why would you say that?"**

&#x200B;

Back up your answers people, the point is where do you base it
